notes: >-
  The epic gate's re-walk, and it earned its keep: five isolated finders over the whole range,
  eleven candidates, eleven fresh verifiers, three verified real - and the one that mattered is a
  defect no WU-level review could have seen.

  W5 gave the core a refusable parameter. W6 built the two-sentence failure model over it, through
  six review rounds. Neither review could see the transition BETWEEN them: refuse a status, then
  type a well-formed one whose request comes back with no answer, and refresh's non-refusal arm set
  silent while leaving refused untouched - so the row region kept quoting "4xz is not a status"
  while the box held 200, a value the core never judged and never refused. The verifier reproduced
  it against the shipped hook before confirming it. Fixed on this tip in the arm that learns
  nothing: a refusal survives silence on the value it was asked with and goes when the box has moved
  on. Pinned RED first, with its pair asserted beside it so a future overcorrection that clears the
  refusal on ANY silence is caught - that pair is W6's round-3 ruling and it still holds. A second
  review over the fix confirmed the updater form is required rather than stylistic (refresh is
  memoised on [api], so a direct read would go stale), that the generation guard gates both writes
  identically, and that onDown is correctly left alone.

  The two remaining verified findings are waived above with their reasons; both are recorded where a
  reader will meet them rather than only here.

  Round 3 covers one further commit, added after the fix when the epic could not be pushed. The
  pre-push walk judged the tip - a code commit - at commit level, where the epic-level notes the
  merge gate demands read as the wrong level plus a phantom doc/v1 path per doc the epic touched.
  That is not a defect this epic introduced: verify-dod range 541fa55 e7e787f fails today on
  E-REDESIGN's own tip. The review of that commit re-derived the mechanism from the gate source
  rather than the prose - range() matches [commit, first] so a three-field merge line falls through
  unmatched, and Gate::verify returns on !gated before the manifest and doc-note checks - reproduced
  the E-REDESIGN failure, and found the thing that made the row worth writing: DEC-2 ALREADY decided
  the tip rule and Gate::walk already implements it, so range() is a decided rule missing at a
  second call site rather than an open question. The row was rewritten around that, and its one
  loose count ("a dozen") went with it. The tip is docs-only, which is what makes the walk pass it.

  Eight of the eleven candidates were refuted, and the refutations are worth as much as the
  findings. The duplicated silent/refused precedence in App.tsx and FlowList.tsx is not duplication:
  it is the deliberate outcome of W6 moving precedence out of the state and into what each zone
  renders, and hoisting it back into one value would re-introduce the mistake five rounds were spent
  undoing. The "epic made only one T1 edit" claim is false - W1 edited component-design.html AND
  design-flow.html - but it stands only in gitignored archived scratch; the tracked doc/v1 note on
  this tip lists both, and its one loose phrase was corrected rather than left to be read as a
  contradiction. The rest were comment-volume and memo-eviction nits that did not survive contact
  with the code.
